## SECTION 4: WHEN ASSURANCE BECOMES DIRECTIVE
*(Upgrade path — explicit, honest)*

**Section headline:** When to upgrade to Directive

Assurance is the right fit for most risk-aware SMBs. But some situations call for more. Consider upgrading to Directive when:

- You receive a HIPAA audit notice or a covered entity partner sends you a BAA request
- Your board or leadership has asked for a formal risk report or security briefing
- An EU regulatory body or customer has asked for NIS2 or DORA documentation
- A customer or prospect requires a SOC 2 report or ISO 27001 certificate
- You've had a security incident — breach, ransomware, phishing — and need a formal IR program
- Your M365 or AWS environment has grown significantly and ad-hoc management is no longer sufficient

Foundation and Assurance clients can upgrade to Directive at any time. Scope and pricing are re-evaluated at the engagement level.

